<title>USA: Vitro trading buy reinstated.</title>
<headline>Vitro trading buy reinstated.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Caspian Securities Inc has reinstated its trading buy rating on Vitro SA, Caspian analyst Martin Lara said on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Lara cited Vitro's letter of intent to sell a 49 percent stake in its Vitrocrisa subsidiary and 100 percent of its Worldcrisa subsidiary to Libbey Inc.</p>
<p>-- Lara also noted a &quot;healthy adjustment&quot; to Vitro stock on recent news of weak fourth-quarter results.</p>
<p>-- The Mexico City glassmaker's ADRs ended unchanged at 8 on Monday.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
</text>
